  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main 7e3c75f9, which includes #1092).\n\n## What changed\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`, non-RTCP indexing path in `tilt()` only: the A word is now written through #1092's `angleWord(\"A\", ...)`, and `missingLetter` runs first. A turning letter the machine does not state is refused by name (\"indexed move commands A - the machine states no A rotary\"), and no word is posted. A stated C that turns is refused by name too (\"indexed move commands C - this dialect's indexing path writes only an A rotary\"). Before this change that path dropped C silently.\n- On a machine that states A, the output is byte-identical: `angleWord` is `w()`, which is `\"A\" + fu(v)` for the finite angle `tilt()` already requires.\n- Other direct rotary-letter writers: there are none left. Doosan's probe macro `ax + fu(pos)` writes only X/Y/Z, and fanuc.cps's non-RTCP path refuses every tilt.\n- The edit stays inside the indexing block, so it merges additively with the open doosan-dnm PRs #961, #981 and #1034 (coolant, units and probe coolant, in other sections).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1155-doosan-index-a-word.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- Pinning test `doosan_dnm_post::doosan_dnm_index_names_only_a_stated_rotary` (app). It checks three things. An A index on a machine with no rotaries is refused by name, with no A word. A turning C on millturn.mch (states C, non-RTCP) is refused by name, with no C word. On the shipped doosan-dnm.mch the motion lines are exactly `M11 / G00 X0 Y0 Z10 A90 / M10 / G01 X50 Y0 Z-1 F400`. I confirmed it fails on the upstream script: no warning, and the A word was posted.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. It ran only the changed test, because .cps is not gate-mapped.\n- By hand: every `camcraft-post` suite passed (all `script_*`, recorded_streams, cycle_hop, post_engine, vendor_mch_cli). These app suites passed: doosan_dnm_post 9, fanuc_post 12, fourth_axis_pose 9, conformance 6, tilt 8, rotary_verify 9, probe_spindle_stop 2, post_unit_word 5, recorded_post_streams 2.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test doosan_dnm_post -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No golden moved.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real Doosan control was used.\n- C indexing on a C table is refused for now, not implemented.\n\nChangelog: doosan-dnm post refuses by name an indexed move that turns a rotary the machine does not state (or a turning C, which the indexing path never wrote) instead of posting an A word the control lacks or silently dropping C (#1155)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1155\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
